**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** What each parameter of a crystal record is as a tensor component, and which principal axis a plate puts on its normal, so a look can be judged by the transverse rule (001 §M layer 1 'what each cut sees'; the S14.1 brief 'REUSE MuellerInverse.internalAngle, gyrationProjection and orientForCut'; `MuellerInverse.fs:62`'s module header: a wave only ever sees the tensor components transverse to its own propagation direction). The cut geometry REUSES `orientForCut` (`MuellerInverse.fs:orientForCut`), and a layer's orientation the rotation the system builder applies (`Propagation.fs:ResolvedLayer.getLayer`, `layer.rotate this.orientation.toRotation`, i.e. `OpticalProperties.rotate`, `MaterialProperties.fs:187`), so the Planner restates no rotation. In `PlannerSymmetry.fs`, after step 465's declarations, each doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S14.1: (1) `CrystalAxis` = `FirstCrystalAxis | SecondCrystalAxis | ThirdCrystalAxis`, a principal axis of the frame the crystal records are written in (`CrystalPhysics.fs`, step 353). `static member marker : OpticalProperties`: the engine properties of a probe crystal, `TriclinicParameters` with `index1 = RefractionIndex 1.0`, `index2 = RefractionIndex 2.0`, `index3 = RefractionIndex 3.0` and every gyration component `RhoValue 0.0`, through its `opticalProperties` (steps 333, 353), so its permittivity is diag(1, 4, 9) and each axis is recognised by its own value wherever a rotation carries it. `static member normalOf (oriented : OpticalProperties) : CrystalAxis option`: the axis whose marker value (1, 4 or 9) equals the real part of `oriented.eps.[2, 2]` (`Eps.Item`, `MaterialProperties.fs:66`) within 1e-9 while the magnitudes of `oriented.eps.[0, 2]` and `oriented.eps.[1, 2]` are below 1e-9, i.e. the principal axis lying along the lab z-axis, the plate normal along which the system stratifies (`MuellerInverse.fs:orientForCut`'s doc); `None` when no principal axis lies along it. The tolerance is one private value of the module: a rotation by 90 degrees leaves round-off near 1e-16 on the entries it zeroes. (2) `CrystalAxisPair = { firstAxis : CrystalAxis; secondAxis : CrystalAxis }`, a record because a tuple repeating a type is ELEV011. (3) `TensorComponent` = `PrincipalIndexComponent of CrystalAxis list` (a principal index on the axes it occupies: n_o on the 1- and 2-axes of a uniaxial crystal) | `GyrationDiagonalComponent of CrystalAxis list` | `GyrationOffDiagonalComponent of CrystalAxisPair` | `AbsorptionDiagonalComponent of CrystalAxis` (a diagonal component of the absorbing record's ε″) | `AbsorptionOffDiagonalComponent of CrystalAxisPair`, with `member this.axes : CrystalAxis list` (a pair's two axes in order). (4) `CrystalComponent = { name : ParameterName; component : TensorComponent }`, one parameter of a crystal record and the component it is. (5) `type CrystalParameters with member this.components : CrystalComponent list`: the names of `this.parameterAxes` (`Studies.fs`, step 361) in their order, each paired positionally (`List.map2`) with its case's component list, so no parameter name is written a second time (AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'). `UniaxialCrystal`: n_o `PrincipalIndexComponent [ FirstCrystalAxis; SecondCrystalAxis ]`, n_e `PrincipalIndexComponent [ ThirdCrystalAxis ]`, g11 `GyrationDiagonalComponent [ FirstCrystalAxis; SecondCrystalAxis ]`, g33 `GyrationDiagonalComponent [ ThirdCrystalAxis ]`. `TriclinicCrystal`: n1, n2 and n3 the index on the 1-, 2- and 3-axis; g11, g22 and g33 the gyration diagonal on each; g23, g13 and g12 the off-diagonals on (2, 3), (1, 3) and (1, 2). `AbsorbingTriclinicCrystal`: the three indices; e11, e22 and e33 `AbsorptionDiagonalComponent` on each axis; e23, e13 and e12 `AbsorptionOffDiagonalComponent` on (2, 3), (1, 3) and (1, 2); then the six gyration components as the triclinic record has them (`MuellerInverse.fs:AbsorbingTriclinicParameters`' axes order). (6) `type SampleCut with member this.normalAxisOpt : CrystalAxis option` (`MuellerInverse.fs:SampleCut`): `CrystalAxis.normalOf (orientForCut this (SampleAzimuth.degree 0.0<Berreman.Constants.deg>) CrystalAxis.marker)`, so `ZCut` answers the 3-axis, `XCut` the 1-axis and `YCut` the 2-axis (the transverse planes `BiaxialInverseTests.fs:135-140` lists), and a `TiltedCut` off 0 and 90 degrees none; the azimuth turns a plate about its normal and never changes the axis on it. (7) `type CrystalOrientation with member this.normalAxisOpt : CrystalAxis option` (`ElementId.fs:CrystalOrientation`): `CrystalAxis.normalOf (CrystalAxis.marker.rotate this.toRotation)` (`ElementId.fs:115`); `PrimaryAxes` is the identity rotation, so a plate of a crystal in its own frame is a z-cut, as `orientForCut ZCut` is. No other member is added. Tests, in `PlannerSymmetryTests` (step 465), over its test-local records: `every crystal record names its parameters' tensor components in its axis order`: each crystal's `components` names equal its `parameterAxes` names in order; the uniaxial components are the four above; the triclinic g23, g13 and g12 are `GyrationOffDiagonalComponent` of the pairs (2, 3), (1, 3) and (1, 2); the absorbing crystal has fifteen components whose seventh to ninth are `AbsorptionOffDiagonalComponent`s and whose last three are `GyrationOffDiagonalComponent`s. `each principal cut puts on the normal the axis orientForCut carries there, and a tilted cut puts none`: `ZCut`, `XCut` and `YCut` answer `ThirdCrystalAxis`, `FirstCrystalAxis` and `SecondCrystalAxis`; `TiltedCut (Angle.degree 30.0<Berreman.Constants.deg>)` answers `None`; and the real part of `CrystalAxis.marker.eps.[i, i]` is 1, 4 and 9 for i = 0, 1, 2. `a plate's crystal orientation puts its axis on the normal as the system builder rotates it`: `PrimaryAxes` answers `ThirdCrystalAxis`; an `EulerRotation` under `ZmYpXp` with phi = psi = 0 and theta = 90 degrees (the rotation `Rotation.rotateY` builds, `Geometry.fs:584`, which `orientForCut XCut` applies) answers `FirstCrystalAxis`; and one with theta = 30 degrees answers `None`.

**Acceptance.** After the components and the cut geometry land, `CrystalParameters.components` MUST name every record parameter's tensor component in its axes' order, and `SampleCut.normalAxisOpt` and `CrystalOrientation.normalAxisOpt` MUST answer the principal axis that `orientForCut` and the layer rotation carry onto the plate normal; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every crystal record names its parameters' tensor components in its axis order`, `each principal cut puts on the normal the axis orientForCut carries there, and a tilted cut puts none` and `a plate's crystal orientation puts its axis on the normal as the system builder rotates it`, the count rising by 3; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s45 invariants MUST pass.
